.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; UP-Term-python install: Python 3.14 in UP-Term:Python3
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, stops the install when UP-Term.lha is
; missing or too old (the reason is in ENV:UPTCHECK).
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/check.dos
Lab copy-python
; Python 3.14 (README): UP-Term:Python3, its programs run as Python3:bin/python3 or
; python3 from vsh (vshrc's path); Python3: is assigned at every boot (a marked
; block in S:User-Startup, the next part).
MakeDir >NIL: UP-Term:Python3
Copy python3 UP-Term:Python3 ALL CLONE QUIET
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
Lab python
Assign Python3: UP-Term:Python3
Search >NIL: S:User-Startup ";BEGIN UP-Term python"
If WARN
  If NOT EXISTS S:User-Startup.before-UP-Term
    Copy S:User-Startup S:User-Startup.before-UP-Term CLONE
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";BEGIN UP-Term python"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "Assign Python3: UP-Term:Python3"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";END UP-Term python"
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "Python installed: type  python3  in an UP-Term window (vsh)."
